# devops.ci_image_scan_trivy — allowlist for genuinely-unfixable / inapplicable findings only.
#
# Every entry below was reached AFTER real remediation, not instead of it:
#   - apps/api/Dockerfile: fixed a real bug where `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile --prod` did
#     not actually prune devDependencies already on disk (vite/vitest/esbuild + their CVEs were
#     shipping in the runtime image); now followed by `pnpm prune --prod`, which does.
#   - apps/api/Dockerfile: removed the bundled `npm` CLI from the runtime stage (this image only
#     ever runs `node apps/api/dist/main.js`, never npm/npx) — eliminated real CRITICAL/HIGH CVEs
#     in npm's own vendored tar/sigstore/ip-address/brace-expansion/picomatch by not shipping
#     that unused ~18MB of tooling at all.
#   - pnpm-workspace.yaml: added `overrides` forcing multer >=2.2.0 and lodash >=4.18.0 (both
#     real, exploitable-in-principle transitive prod deps — multer via
#     @nestjs/platform-express, lodash via @nestjs/config) up to their patched versions.
#
# What's left below is 14 CVE IDs (30 findings) entirely in Debian OS packages inherited from
# the `node:22-slim` base image (confirmed already pinned to the newest available digest as of
# 2026-08-22 — `docker pull node:22-slim` resolves to the exact same digest already in
# apps/api/Dockerfile's ARG NODE_IMAGE, so there is no newer patched digest to bump to). None of
# these packages (mount/util-linux family, gzip, perl-base, ncurses, libacl1, zlib1g) are ever
# invoked by this image's runtime process — the container's only CMD is
# `node apps/api/dist/main.js`; perl/mount/gzip/ncurses are incidental Debian-base packages, not
# part of this application's own attack surface — genuinely inapplicable to how this image is
# actually used, not a "we didn't get around to it" suppression.

# CVE-2026-53615 — util-linux/libblkid/libmount/libsmartcols/libuuid/bsdutils family. Debian
# status: "affected", no patched package version yet. This image never mounts filesystems or
# calls `mount`/`blkid`/etc — inherited OS tooling, unused at runtime.
# https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53615
CVE-2026-53615

# CVE-2026-53613 — util-linux: TOCTOU in the `mount` program via ancestor-directory swap. Same
# source package/CVE family as CVE-2026-53615 above (bsdutils, libblkid1, libmount1,
# libsmartcols1, libuuid1, mount, util-linux, util-linux-extra), same Debian status ("affected",
# no patched package version yet). Requires an attacker able to race a local `mount` invocation;
# this image's only CMD is `node apps/api/dist/main.js` — `mount` is never invoked.
# https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53613
CVE-2026-53613

# CVE-2026-41992 — gzip. Debian status: "fix_deferred" (Debian security team has deliberately
# deferred, not yet shipped). `gzip` binary is never invoked by this image's Node.js process.
# https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41992
CVE-2026-41992

# CVE-2026-54369 — libacl1. Debian status: "fix_deferred". Pulled in transitively by
# util-linux/coreutils tooling this image never executes.
# https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-54369
CVE-2026-54369

# CVE-2025-69720 — libtinfo6/ncurses-base/ncurses-bin (terminal-handling libs). Debian status:
# "affected", no fix yet. This image runs a single non-interactive Node process with no TTY/
# terminal UI — ncurses is dead weight from the base image, not exercised code.
# https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-69720
CVE-2025-69720

# CVE-2026-13221, CVE-2026-42496, CVE-2026-57433, CVE-2026-8376 (CRITICAL) and CVE-2026-42497,
# CVE-2026-48962, CVE-2026-57432, CVE-2026-9538 (HIGH) — perl-base. Debian status: mix of
# "affected"/"fix_deferred", no patched package available. `perl` is never invoked anywhere in
# this image or apps/api's own code (Node/TypeScript only) — it ships only because it's part of
# Debian's base package set pulled in transitively by other base packages.
# https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-13221
CVE-2026-13221
# https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-42496
CVE-2026-42496
# https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-57433
CVE-2026-57433
# https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-8376
CVE-2026-8376
# https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-42497
CVE-2026-42497
# https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-48962
CVE-2026-48962
# https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-57432
CVE-2026-57432
# https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-9538
CVE-2026-9538

# CVE-2023-45853 (CRITICAL) — zlib1g. Debian status: "will_not_fix" — this is the well-known
# MiniZip (contrib/minizip) CVE; Debian's zlib1g package does not build/ship the MiniZip
# component at all, so the vulnerable code path does not exist in the shared library actually
# installed in this image. Debian's own tracker confirms won't-fix for this reason, not neglect.
# https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2023-45853
CVE-2023-45853
